// An array as a value, `method int inc(int n) { return n + 1 } initial state A do x = inc(a) go to A`. KIELER rejects
// it: assignment to ‘int’ from ‘int *’ makes integer from pointer without a cast [-Wint-conversion].
scchart Main { input bool b input int i int a[2] = {4,7} int c[2] = {4,7} int m[2][2] = {{4,7},{8,1}} float fa[2] bool ba[2] output int x output float f output bool y method int inc(int n) { return n + 1 } initial state A do x = inc(a) go to A }
